.TH JOY-PI-BOARD 1 "2026-10-19" "Joy Pi Board 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
joy-pi-board \- present Joy Pi Health observations on a local network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B joy-pi-board
.RI [ "\-\-listen IP:port" ]
.RI [ "\-\-health-url URL" ]
.RB [ \-\-diagnostic-timing ]
.br
.B joy-pi-board \-\-help
.br
.B joy-pi-board \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Joy Pi Board serves an embedded web dashboard and a read-only overview API.
It presents observations from Joy Pi Health and does not collect system metrics
or access sensors. The interface starts and remains available when Health is
unavailable. No Node runtime, external asset server or local asset directory is
required.
.SH OPTIONS
Options may appear only once. Unknown options and positional arguments are
rejected. Value options accept either a separate argument or an equals sign.
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " IP:port"
Bind to a numeric IPv4 or bracketed IPv6 address and a decimal port from 0 to
65535. Port 0 requests an automatically assigned port. Default: 0.0.0.0:8081.
Use an unprivileged port with the packaged service.
.TP
.BI \-\-health-url " URL"
Health snapshot URL. Requires HTTP, an explicit host and port from 1 to 65535,
and the path /v1/snapshot. Credentials, queries and fragments are forbidden.
Default: http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1/snapshot.
.TP
.B \-\-diagnostic-timing
Temporarily emit bounded request timing diagnostics to the log output.
Disabled by default; takes no value and has no environment equivalent.
At most 4096 request records are admitted per process, with loss and truncation
counters. Missing, dropped or truncated samples invalidate measurements.
There is no diagnostic endpoint, system collector or internal persistence.
This option cannot be combined with help or version.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Print help and exit without binding or contacting Health. Must stand alone.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version, revision and build time, then exit without binding or contacting
Health. Must stand alone. A target version does not imply release acceptance.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B JOY_PI_BOARD_LISTEN
and
.B JOY_PI_BOARD_HEALTH_URL
provide the corresponding option values. An explicit flag takes precedence
over a present environment variable, which takes precedence over the default.
An empty value is invalid. Help and version do not validate these variables.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/joy-pi-board
Administrator configuration, read by the packaged systemd unit as an
EnvironmentFile. It uses systemd syntax and is not sourced as a shell script.
Direct invocation of the binary does not read this file.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/joy-pi-board.service
Packaged service running as the dedicated unprivileged joy-pi-board account.
Installation does not enable or start it; authorized operators choose these
actions explicitly. There is no Health startup dependency.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/joy-pi-board/
Operation guide, build provenance, asset inventory and third-party notices.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Logs go to standard error; the packaged service sends them to journald.
Default logging covers lifecycle and significant provider transitions.
SIGINT and SIGTERM initiate graceful shutdown under a five-second budget.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates normal completion. 2 indicates invalid startup configuration.
1 indicates another failure, such as inability to bind the listener.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR systemd.exec (5),
.BR journalctl (1)
